  "label": "Sea-Monkeys toy product",
  "description": "Sea-Monkeys is a brand name for brine shrimp (Artemia) sold as novelty aquarium pets. Marketed since the 1960s, they were advertised as instant pets that come to life when added to water. The product featured cartoon illustrations of humanoid creatures, though the actual organisms are tiny crustaceans. This commercial product reference is essential to understanding the racist comparison being made in the meme.",
